    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d69">

                <pb facs="0169" n="141" sameAs="frus:frus1964-68v20/pg141"/>

                <head>69. Memorandum From Secretary of Defense McNamara to President Johnson<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d69-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1968-02-06">February 6, 1968</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>You have asked that I inform you of “the latest date on which the President could
                    make a decision to supply Israel with Phantom aircraft of appropriate
                    configuration to be delivered to Israel beginning in January 1970.”</p>
                <p>If your decision is made on or before December 31, 1968, we can begin the
                    delivery of Phantoms to Israel in January 1970. The Israeli request was for 50
                    aircraft. We would plan to deliver them at the rate of approximately 4 per
                    month.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Robert S. McNamara</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
